LRC14 pair-good decoy classifier
========================================================================
Assumption challenge
  Candidate vertex sets considered:
    runners, gaps, fixed sections, section boundaries, wall crossings,
    residues, cover arcs, Fourier modes, matroid circuits, proof obligations,
    active normal-fan owners, and decoy generator triples.
  Chosen vertex set:
    generator triples (source pair lane, blocker residue tooth, blocker deck).
  Preserved LRC predicate:
    pair-good candidate is harmless exactly when every blocker residue tooth
    is outside threshold; decoy means at least one tooth inequality is strict.
  Destroyed by raw counts:
    which blocker tooth generated the failure and whether many times share one mechanism.

[0] Exact generator lemma
  For t=p/q in lowest terms, runner c blocks iff
    14 * min(c*p mod q, q-(c*p mod q)) < q.
  A pair-good decoy is exactly a source pair lane plus at least one such
  blocker tooth.  Counts are therefore shadows of modular tooth families.

