[3] Why the count is not the invariant
  The largest rows have thousands of decoys because many source pairs cross
  inside the same small set of blocker tooth regimes.  The proof object is
  the blocker residue inequality, not the number of candidate times hitting it.
  Packet sidecar fields suggested:
    decoy_source_lane, decoy_source_shell, decoy_blocker_role,
    decoy_blocker_depth_bucket, decoy_zero_tooth_flag,
    decoy_generator_cover_size, decoy_top_generator_key.

[4] Tournament Analysis
  vertices are generator/proof carriers, not runners.
  pairwise observable:
    predicate exactness, modular checkability, denominator retention,
    normal-fan compatibility, family compression, and anti-count guard.
  switch:
    majority comparison of these coordinates; ties use the listed path.
  score_hist=[(0, 1), (1, 1), (2, 1), (3, 1), (4, 1), (5, 1), (6, 1), (7, 1)]
  directed_3cycles=0
  hamiltonian_path_count=1
  tie_hamiltonian_path=blocker_residue_tooth_inequality > source_pair_lane_plus_blocker_deck > normal_fan_active_owner_support > family_compressed_generator_cover > near_wall_clearance_margin > zero_tooth_divisibility_subcase > raw_decoy_count > raw_pair_gap
